## Goal
Write a single scene of the novel in full prose, as a seamless continuation of the text above.

## Requirements
{{#if skills}}
- The Skill Documents at the top are the grounding truth of this scene: follow them as authoritative instructions, not as background reading.
{{/if}}
{{#if writing_styles}}
- The Writing styles References&Instructions above tell you how this scene must read: follow the diction, rhythm, and imagery they show rather than writing in a neutral default voice.
{{/if}}
{{#if writing_constraints}}
- The Writing Constrains above are binding, not advisory: each one must hold across the whole scene — a scene that breaks one is a failed scene, however well written.
{{/if}}
- Write exactly the scene defined by its Title and Description above; the Description is the entire extent of this scene — stay inside it and do not advance other plotlines or skip ahead in time.
- Stop the prose at the Description's last beat. Later scenes continue the story from exactly there, so never write past that point: nobody arrives, returns, leaves, wakes or falls asleep, no journey or errand ends, no time or place shifts, and nothing is packed away, tidied or cleared up.
- Whatever the Description leaves open stays open: an unfinished action stays unfinished — a mouth still full, a hand still held, a question still unanswered — and must not be resolved or completed.
- When the Description ends in a state or mood, end the prose inside it: your closing paragraph must add no event of its own. Re-read that last paragraph before answering and drop anything that reaches beyond the Description.
- Keep every character consistent with their established traits, speech patterns, and motivations, and honor the story's start and end states.
- The novel text above is everything written so far: match its narrative voice, tense, and point of view, continue seamlessly from where it ends, and never repeat or contradict it. Your prose will be appended directly after it.
- Output ONLY the scene prose as plain paragraphs — no headings, no title, no explanations.

Respond entirely in "{{ language }}".

